# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform.
#
# A CRLF shebang makes the interpreter "not found" inside a Linux container --
# the script exists, is executable, and still fails. It cost one debugging cycle
# on the dashboard entrypoint; this makes it impossible to reintroduce by
# checking the repository out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
